{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cesk6sseFek6xWAeJKJQp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## ANALYSIS\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nAdd a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions shipments from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED` status, treats retries (already confirmed) as idempotent success, rejects cancellation of confirmed shipments with 409, and rejects unknown shipment IDs with 404.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `ShipmentController.kt:21-56` — existing controller with create, getById, and list endpoints\n- `Shipment.kt:9-33` — data model with `ShipmentStatus` enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `InMemoryShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — in-memory store with save, findById, and existsById methods\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:11-30` — `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) and `ConflictException` (409) exception types\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — `ErrorCode` enum with existing codes: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-29` — centralized exception-to-response handler\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — integration tests using MockMvc\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses; `GlobalExceptionHandler` converts to `ApiError` response envelope\n- Status codes are determined by exception type: `ResourceNotFoundException` → 404, `ConflictException` → 409\n- Controllers directly use repositories; no separate service layer\n- Status transitions are simple: load, update field, save\n- Tests use MockMvc with `jsonPath` assertions on `$.error.code` for machine-readable codes\n- `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(saved)` pattern for successful creates\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add the `/confirm` POST endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` — must add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED` error code to distinguish this conflict case from others\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add four new tests covering the four requirement cases\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Idempotent retry logic — confirming an already-confirmed shipment must not fail\n2. State machine enforcement — rejecting transitions from invalid states (CANCELLED)\n3. Persistence — the confirmed state must survive the save/retrieve cycle in the repository\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone identified. The ticket is explicit about what states must be handled, what status codes to return, and that retries must succeed.\n\n---\n\n## DESIGN\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED` error code to the enum. This makes the error machine-readable for clients.\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`** — Add method:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment\n   ```\n   The method will:\n   - Fetch the shipment by ID; throw `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found (404 case)\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throw `ConflictException` with the new error code (409 case)\n   - If status is `CREATED`, update it to `CONFIRMED` and save\n   - If status is already `CONFIRMED`, do nothing and return the shipment unchanged (idempotent case)\n   - Return the (possibly unchanged) shipment with HTTP 200\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`** — Add four new tests:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions it to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without changing it\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with the correct error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with the correct error code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered whether to add a service layer between controller and repository (e.g., `ShipmentService.confirm()`), but the existing code shows controllers directly calling repositories for simple operations like this. Adding a service layer would be unnecessary refactoring outside the scope of this ticket.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Return | Via |\n|------|------|-------|--------|-----|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | `findById()` returns shipment | `save()` with status=CONFIRMED | 200 Shipment | return |\n| CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED (retry) | `findById()` returns shipment | (none) | 200 Shipment | return |\n| CANCELLED | `findById()` returns shipment | (none) | 409 error envelope | `ConflictException` → `GlobalExceptionHandler` |\n| Not found | `findById()` returns null | (none) | 404 error envelope | `ResourceNotFoundException` → `GlobalExceptionHandler` |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **`confirms a created shipment`** — Create shipment, confirm it, assert status=CONFIRMED in response\n2. **`confirms an already confirmed shipment succeeds`** — Confirm once, confirm again, assert both return status 200 and status=CONFIRMED\n3. **`rejects confirming a cancelled shipment`** — Write a CANCELLED shipment directly to repository, attempt confirm, assert 409 with error code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED`\n4. **`rejects confirming a non-existent shipment`** — Attempt confirm on a shipment ID that was never created, assert 404 with error code `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`\n\n---\n\n## IMPLEMENTATION\n\nNow I'll make the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1168,"cache_read_input_tokens":15390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1168},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"602e4904-947d-4bec-bb30-d95c88566eb1","uuid":"7c7504ba-785f-4b5e-add0-7fbd5747a71d","timestamp":"2026-09-09T10:56:08.664Z","request_id":"req_011Cesk6rzJjuEsunChBF5qV"}
